  "question": "Was the Python programming language first released in 1981?",
  "status": "completed",
  "verdict": "refuted",
  "confidence": 0.933,
  "summary": "The claim that the Python programming language was first released in 1981 is refuted by the verified evidence. Two independent sources contradict the claimed date. Evidence ev-1 (centerconsulting.com) states that 'The first public release of Python happened on February 20, 1991, when Guido van Rossum posted version 0.9.0 to the alt.sources newsgroup on Usenet.' Evidence ev-2 (geeksforgeeks.org) corroborates this, stating that 'Python's journey began with version 0.9.0, released by Guido van Rossum in 1991.' Both verified excerpts consistently date Python's initial release to 1991, a decade later than the 1981 date asserted in the claim. No evidence was found supporting a 1981 release, and no conflicts exist between the retrieved sources. The evidence establishes the release year as 1991; the specific day-level date (February 20, 1991) is attested by only one of the two sources.",
